  "question": {
    "text": "If the quadratic equation $a x^2+b x+c=0(a\\gt0)$ has two roots $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ such that $\\alpha \\lt -2$ and $\\beta\\gt2$ then",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "uDHtN",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{c} \\lt 0$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "uKdeZ",
      "text": "$a+b+c\\gt0$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "F8wJD",
      "text": "$a-b+c \\lt 0$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "t0lhY",
      "text": "$a-b+c\\gt0$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hint: $f(x)=a x^2+b x+c$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/zsWJNifUkpZT6pK2zwwxGA5t3n74wW4RIZ5NQqHVMDo.original.fullsize.png\"/>\nso, $f(-2) \\lt 0$ and $f(2)\\gt0$\nalso, $f(0) \\lt 0 \\Rightarrow c \\lt 0$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& f(-1) \\lt 0 \\Rightarrow a-b+c \\lt 0 \\\\\n& f(1) \\lt 0 \\Rightarrow a+b+c \\lt 0\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
